# Vendored native binaries (tilemaker). Fetched by npm run setup:tools.
tools/

# Source extracts and every built artifact. Regenerate with npm run build-city.
data/
*.osm.pbf
*.pmtiles
*.mbtiles

# ONE exception, deliberately narrow. A few real blobs sliced out of an extract, committed
# so the decoder has at least one test against actual bytes rather than only against
# synthetic fixtures that share its own assumptions. 1.23 MB as sliced: one OSMHeader plus
# the first dense-node, first way and first relation block. Size is asserted by
# tests/pipeline/real-bytes.test.ts so a careless regeneration cannot commit an extract.
# Regenerate with npm run make:fixture.
# This is NOT a licence to commit an extract or a built artifact: hard-rules.md still bans
# those, and the reason it gives (hundreds of MB, reproducible from config) is exactly why
# this narrow slice does not fall under it.
!tests/pipeline/fixtures/real-slice.osm.pbf

